      "evidence": "practice R1 (rows one at a time, 10 cores): rerank 1,250 ms mean, dense search 6 ms, end-to-end 1,286 vs 143 ms (baseline) and 207 ms (RAPTOR). test R2: generation 84-90 s mean per question, so the rerank's 0.9 s is about 1 % of end-to-end. One-time costs: RAPTOR-tree summaries US$1.46 and 439 calls (plan 030); reranker download 88 MB (MiniLM) or 1.1 GB (bge).",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
